meta {
  name: Bulk Edit Branch Lab Panels
  type: http
  seq: 11
}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/branch-lab-panels/bulk
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "data": [
      {
        "id": "{{branchLabPanelId}}",
        "isActive": false,
        "priceMsrp": 3000,
        "priceMaximum": 2800,
        "priceMinimum": 2000,
        "isHomeCollection": true
      }
    ]
  }
}

vars:pre-request {
  branchLabPanelId: 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
}

tests {
  test("200 OK", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });
  test("reports updated count", function () {
    const data = res.getBody() && res.getBody().data;
    expect(data).to.have.property("updated");
  });
}

docs {
  Bulk-edit the active branch's Lab Panel List: `data` is an array of per-row
  edits, each carrying its own `id` plus the branch-tunable fields to change
  **for that row** (scoped to the caller's tenant + active branch). Only the
  rows in the payload are touched. Returns `{ updated: <count> }`.

  ## Rules

  - `data` — 1 to 500 items. Each item's `id` must resolve to an active branch
    lab panel in the caller's tenant + active branch; an unresolved id → 404
    `BRANCH_LAB_PANEL_NOT_FOUND`.
  - Each item may set any subset of the same branch-tunable fields as the
    single-row `PUT /branch-lab-panels/:id` (pricing, applicability, TAT,
    flags, instructions, status). Identity (`panelName`/`panelCode`) and
    member-test composition are **not** bulk-editable — those are managed via
    re-import/sync.
  - **All-or-nothing**: a duplicate `id`, an item with no changes, or a broken
    price ordering (min ≤ max ≤ msrp, re-checked per row against its existing
    values) → 422 `VALIDATION_ERROR` and **nothing** is changed. Updates run in
    one transaction.
  - Note: a later **sync** overwrites any bulk edits made to imported originals.
}
